abstract: >-
  Machine-checked Lean 4 formalizations over Mathlib of the improved sunflower
  bounds, an upper bound on the metric TSP subtour-LP integrality gap,
  Shamir's IP = PSPACE theorem, Toda's theorem PH ⊆ P^#P, and the PCP theorem
  NP = PCP(O(log n), O(1)).
  The sunflower development includes Alweiss–Lovett–Wu–Zhang, Rao–Bell–Chueluecha–Warnke,
  robust-sunflower lower bounds and Erdős–Rado. The TSP development follows
  Karlin–Klein–Oveis Gharan, Gurvits–Klein–Leake and Song, and proves the
  existence, on at least three vertices, of a tour of cost at most
  (3/2 - 2.05522e-30) times any feasible subtour-LP objective.
  IPPSPACE proves the unconditional class equality using unchanged Complexitylib
  definitions, a uniform polynomial-time reduction, and a certified interactive
  verifier. The reverse inclusion is imported from Complexitylib; unchanged
  upstream sources retain their attribution.
  Toda proves PH ⊆ P^#P from Complexitylib's unchanged PH and #P definitions to
  a full-binary-answer oracle machine class, following Fortnow's isolation and
  amplification route with machine-level counting closure and costed queries.
  PCP proves NP ⊆ PCP(O(log n), O(1)) with a polynomial-time verifier certified
  on Mathlib's Turing machines, and the converse, following the algebraic proof
  of Amireddy, Behera, Srinivasan, Sudan and Willumsgaard without PCP
  composition. It includes proofs of the ALMSS point-versus-line theorem and the
  Arora–Safra bivariate agreement lemma, and identifies its NP class with
  Complexitylib's unchanged definition.
  The shared build includes axiom checks and regression
  examples. Documentation records the scope and adaptations of the proofs.
